<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasdai ibn Shaprut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 915–c. 975</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasdai ibn Shaprut was a Jewish physician, diplomat and patron at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hakam-ii">al-Hakam II</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He received foreign embassies, helped prepare an Arabic version of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedanius-dioscorides">Dioscorides</a>' De materia medica and treated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-i-of-leon">Sancho I of León</a>. As leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> he patronised the scholars who began the golden age of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> poetry and grammar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p></div>
